==English==

===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|certeynte|lang=enm|surety}}, from {{etyl|xno|en}} {{term|certeinte|certeinté||lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|certeinete|certeineté|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|VL.|-}} *{{term||certanitas|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|certus|lang=la}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-certainty.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|certainties}}

# The state of being [[certain]].
#* Fisher Ames
#*: The '''certainty''' of punishment is the truest security against crimes.
# An instance of being certain.
# A fact or truth unquestionably established.
#* Landor
#*: '''Certainties''' are uninteresting and sating.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|state of being certain}} [[certitude]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|state of being certain}} [[uncertainty]]

